I think we've located another bug the hard way :-( (luckely it wasn't me ;-)
The situation: a player arrived at the castle. As he didn't have any musical
instrument, nor could he find it in the whole dungeon, he tried to fill the
moat with rocks. His thought was: "If one boulder (`) can fill the moat,
then also enough rocks (*) created from this one (or even more) boulders
should also fill the moat". So he started looking for boulders, chopped them
into pieces and filled the moat. At a certain point he did indeed saw the
moat disappear and a * was shown on the screen (also if using the \ key)
Now he stepped on it and died immediately, as he couldn't swim.
Now the question is: is this wrong, i.e. if the moat is completely filled
with small *'s, then one should be able to cross over it. Also: is it
possible to fill the moat with rocks ?
I tried to reconstruct this in debug mode, and yes: this can be done. However
a rock is only displayed when it hits an eel. Maybe that's what happened.
Shouldn't the screen be still showing a "{" in stead of a "*" in this case ?
For the record: we are playing NetHack 3.0, PL10 on Unix System V.2.
